## Why This Is Asked

Assesses the ability to design a scalable, auditable cross-tenant security workflow with concrete automation points across DevOps, container registries, policy enforcement, and cross-tenant governance.

## Key Concepts

- Artifact signing and image provenance verification
- Azure Container Registry content trust implementation
- Azure Policy enforcement for supply-chain controls
- Azure Lighthouse cross-tenant approval workflows
- Immutable tagging strategies and automated rollback capabilities

## Code Example

```json
{
  "policyDefinition": {
    "name": "RequireSignedImages",
    "properties": {
      "description": "Enforces signed container images for AKS deployments",
      "policyRule": {
        "if": {
          "field": "type",
          "equals": "Microsoft.ContainerService/managedClusters"
        },
        "then": {
          "effect": "deny",
          "details": [
            {
              "field": "Microsoft.ContainerService/managedClusters/addonProfiles.omsagent.enabled",
              "equals": true
            }
          ]
        }
      }
    }
  }
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
This question validates the ability to design an automated security response system for multi-tenant Azure SaaS environments, integrating threat detection with immediate containment and recovery capabilities.

## Key Concepts
- Anomaly detection using Defender for Cloud analytics and Sentinel ML models
- Event Grid-based alert routing and per-tenant processing
- Automated resource isolation via NSG rules, private endpoint restrictions, and conditional access policies
- Key Vault credential rotation and token revocation workflows
- Deployment slot rollback with feature flag coordination
- Comprehensive audit trails across all security actions

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-logic for automated breach response
async function handleSecurityAlert(alert) {
  if (alert.severity > 3) {
    await isolateTenantResources(alert.tenantId);
    await rotateCompromisedCredentials(alert.tenantId);
    await initiateSafeRollback(alert.tenantId);
  }
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Assess storage security, policy enforcement, and rollback capabilities in a practical scenario.

## Key Concepts
- Azure Policy deny public network access
- Private Endpoints and VNET integration
- Managed Identities RBAC
- Secrets in Key Vault instead of config

## Code Example
```json
{
  "mode": "Indexed",
  "policyRule": {
    "if": {
      "allOf": [
        {"field": "type", "equals": "Microsoft.Storage/storageAccounts"},
        {"field": "properties.publicNetworkAccess", "equals": "Enabled"}
      ]
    },
    "then": {"effect": "deny"}
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you validate rollback after applying policy?
- How would you handle temporary public access needs during migrations?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to design automated IR in Azure at scale, integrating Key Vault, Sentinel, Runbooks, and network isolation.

## Key Concepts

- Key Vault rotation and secret versioning
- Azure Sentinel detection rules and alerting
- Automation Runbooks or Logic Apps
- Private Endpoints and NSGs
- Azure AD session revocation and PIM

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo-IR runbook snippet (Azure SDK)
async function rotateSecret(vaultName, secretName){
  const newValue = generateSecret();
  await secretClient.setSecret(vaultName, secretName, newValue);
  await aadClient.revokeUserSessions('compromised-id');
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you test the rollback path under partial failure?
- How do you ensure no downtime during rotation?

## Why This Is Asked
This probes practical Azure Policy usage, Private Endpoints, tagging discipline, and CI/CD gating with rollback in a beginner-friendly way.

## Key Concepts
- Azure Policy deny public network access for storage accounts
- Private Endpoints and private DNS configuration
- Resource tagging as policy gates in CI/CD
- Rollback to last known-good ARM/Bicep template
- Monitoring and alerting via Azure Monitor

## Code Example
```json
{
  "properties": {
    "displayName": "Deny public network access on storage accounts",
    "policyType": "Regular",
    "mode": "All",
    "policyRule": {
      "if": {
        "allOf": [
          {"field": "type", "equals": "Microsoft.Storage/storageAccounts"},
          {"field": "Microsoft.Storage/storageAccounts/networkAcls/defaultAction", "equals": "Allow"}
        ]
      },
      "then": {"effect": "Deny"}
    }
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you adapt this for multi-region storage and cross-tenant sharing?
- How would you test the CI gate to minimize false positives and ensure rollback works?

